{"subject":"Physiology","sourceTitle":"All In One Online","title":"PrepLadder · 7.Previous Year Questions","deckName":"created by tele @Neet_pg_bot::prep::Qbank::Physiology::7.Previous_Year_Questions","questions":[{"id":"all-in-one-1760436539250","topic":"PrepLadder · 7.Previous Year Questions","number":1,"stem":"A patient reports difficulty switching between movements and experiences uncontrollable hand movements. What is the most likely diagnosis?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Dysdiadochokinesis"},{"label":"B","text":"Intentional Tremor"},{"label":"C","text":"Metamorphosis"},{"label":"D","text":"Resting Tremor"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Dysdiadochokinesis","solutionHtml":"o perform <strong>rapid <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"1b5a7ceea716927771815e7283e571\">alternating</span> movements</strong> (e.g., pronation/supination of the hands). <strong>Difficulty switching between movements</strong> suggests <strong>dysdiadochokinesis (impaired diadochokinesis)</strong>, which is commonly associated with <strong>cerebellar dysfunction</strong> seen in:\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Cerebellar ataxia</strong> (due to stroke, multiple sclerosis, or degenerative disorders)</li>\n<li><strong>Parkinson’s disease</strong> (along with <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"4f6882021f1692777183fa4ca2038d\">bradykinesia</span> and rigidity)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Clinical Features of Cerebellar Diseases</strong></p>\n<table cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:624px\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Hypotonia</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Decreased muscle tone, often on the same side as the cerebellar lesion.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Ataxia</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Uncoordinated movements, often leading to a \"drunken\" gait.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Dysdiadochokinesia</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Inability to perform rapid <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"1b5a7ceea716927771815e7283e571\">alternating</span> movements, such as flipping the hands back and forth.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Dysmetria (Past pointing)</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Movements that overshoot or undershoot the intended target.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Intention tremor</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Tremors occurring when moving toward a target</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Dysarthria</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Jumbled speech due to lack of <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"3820ba101416927771858fe257e119\">coordination</span> in the muscles involved in speech</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Nystagmus</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Rapid, tremulous eye movements</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Rebound Phenomenon</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Limb jerking back after resistance is suddenly removed</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Decomposition of movement</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Can't move multiple joints simultaneously.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>No <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"408bcde7f01692777198acadb8e1c6\">sensory</span> deficit</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Not typically present in cerebellar diseases.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p> </p>\n<p><strong>Intentional <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"bb6d2476421692777200c2af1ac0c8\">Tremor</span> (Option B)</strong> is incorrect because <strong>intention tremor</strong> (seen in cerebellar lesions) appears during <strong>voluntary movement</strong>, worsening as the target is approached, rather than causing difficulty in <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"1b5a7ceea716927771815e7283e571\">alternating</span> movements.</p>\n<p><br/>\n </p>\n<p><strong>Metamorphosis (Option C)</strong> is incorrect because <strong>metamorphopsia</strong> refers to <strong>visual distortions</strong>, not movement abnormalities.</p>\n<p><br/>\n </p>\n<p><strong>Resting <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"bb6d2476421692777200c2af1ac0c8\">Tremor</span> (Option D)</strong> is incorrect because <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"300f03be1a169277719719e4585899\">resting tremor</span> is seen in <strong>Parkinson’s disease</strong>, occurring at rest and improving with voluntary movement, rather than difficulty in switching movements.</p>\n<p> </p><br/><br/><div class=\"quiz-references\">Guyton and Hall Textbook of Medical Physiology, 14th Edition, Page: 719, 720</div>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436539252","topic":"PrepLadder · 7.Previous Year Questions","number":2,"stem":"What nerve fibers are responsible for the transmission of proprioception?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A alpha"},{"label":"B","text":"A beta"},{"label":"C","text":"A gamma"},{"label":"D","text":"A delta"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"A alpha","solutionHtml":"apse; width:780px\"&amp;gt;\n\t<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"8\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:1px solid black\">\n<p><strong>Classification of nerve fibres - Erlanger and Gasser and Lloyd-Hunt </strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p><strong>Fiber Type</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p><strong>Erlanger-Gasser Classification</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p><strong>Lloyd-Hunt Classification</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p><strong>Myelination</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p><strong>Function</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p><strong>Conduction Velocity (m/s)</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p><strong>Diameter (µm)</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p><strong>Sensitivity to Blockade</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>Aα</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>Aα</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>Ia, Ib</p>\n</td>\n<td rowspan=\"5\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>Myelinated</p>\n<p> </p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>Proprioception, <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"3db910d8571692777198303e3bcb27\">somatic</span> motor</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>70-120</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>12-20</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>Pressure - Most susceptible</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>Aβ</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>Aβ</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>II</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>Touch, pressure</p>\n<p><strong>(Option B)</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>30-70</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>5-12</p>\n</td>\n<td rowspan=\"3\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>Pressure - Intermediate.</p>\n<p> </p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>Aγ</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>Aγ</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p> </p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>Motor to muscle spindles</p>\n<p><strong>(Option C)</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>15-30</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>3-6</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>Aδ</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>Aδ</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>III</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>Pain (fast), temperature (cold)</p>\n<p><strong>(Option D)</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>12-30</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>2-5</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>B</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>B</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p> </p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>Preganglionic autonomic</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>3-15</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>&amp;lt;3</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>Hypoxia - Most susceptible</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>C<br/>\n\t\t\t(Dorsal Root)</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>C</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>IV</p>\n</td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>Unmyelinated</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>Pain (slow), temperature (warm)</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>0.5-2</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>0.4-1.2</p>\n</td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>Local anesthetics - Most susceptible</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>C (Sympathetic)</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>C</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p> </p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>Postganglionic sympathetic</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>0.7-2.3</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none\">\n<p>0.3-1.3</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n\n<p> </p><br/><br/><div class=\"quiz-references\">Classification of peripheral nerve fibres. An historical perspective - PubMed (nih.gov)<br/>Ganong’s Review of Medical Physiology (26th edition), Page. 91-92.</div>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436539254","topic":"PrepLadder · 7.Previous Year Questions","number":3,"stem":"Which of the following substances causes a bitter taste that deters us from consuming toxic substances?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Aldehyde"},{"label":"B","text":"Amino acids"},{"label":"C","text":"Alkaloids"},{"label":"D","text":"Hydrogen ions"}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Alkaloids","solutionHtml":"lanation:\n<p><strong>Bitter taste:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Alkaloids are a class of naturally occurring organic compounds that often have bitter tastes.</li>\n<li>Various plants produce them as a defence mechanism against herbivores and insects.</li>\n<li>Many alkaloids are toxic or have pharmacological effects on the human body.</li>\n<li>Examples of alkaloids: are caffeine, nicotine, morphine, and quinine.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Aldehyde (Option A): </strong>Aldehydes and ketones have a sweet taste. Most sweet substances are organic. This option is incorrect.</p>\n<p><strong>Amino acids (Option B):</strong> α-amino acids have a sweet taste, but polypeptides are often bitter. This option is incorrect.</p>\n<p><strong>Hydrogen ions (Option D): </strong>Sour taste is <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"3978e9614f1692777200abbe4cfa34\">triggered</span> by <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"11f7bcb8da16927771898e93932195\">hydrogen</span> ions, the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"fc562fef3f16927771805b9a31499c\">adequate stimulus</span> being a pH of less than 4 of the solution. This option is incorrect.</p><br/><br/><div class=\"quiz-references\">GK Pal Comprehensive Textbook of Medical Physiology, page 1227.</div>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436539256","topic":"PrepLadder · 7.Previous Year Questions","number":4,"stem":"Which of the following is not a characteristic of decerebrate rigidity according to the Herrington classification?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rigidity occurs in all the muscles of the body"},{"label":"B","text":"Increase in the rate of discharge of the γ efferent neuron"},{"label":"C","text":"Increased excitability of the motor neuron pool"},{"label":"D","text":"Mid-collicular lesion can lead to decerebrate rigidity"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Rigidity occurs in all the muscles of the body","solutionHtml":"d=\"45f9bc42ac16927771871c9dc2970a\"&amp;gt;extensor muscles of the limbs, leading to the characteristic <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"115643fed616927771961316effc71\">posture</span> of rigid extension. It does not affect all the muscles of the body equally.\n<p>According to the Herrington classification, <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"a243ecb6401692777186404bdb4792\">decerebrate rigidity</span> is a <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"a1b06f401f1692777203a53393ba98\">form</span> of <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"458e050fdc16927771809854c9fd53\">abnormal</span> muscle tone that occurs due to damage or <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"3662597407169277718640a12868f5\">dysfunction</span> in the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"53abb386551692777192c4d1f1f5ed\">medulla</span> resulting in increased activity of motoneurons that facilitate stretch reflexes.</p>\n<p>Facilitation of stretch reflexes occurs due to two mechanisms:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Increased <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"3892cfe03616927771872f834cf855\">excitability</span> of the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"29e1987f81169277719209260ba0f1\">motor neuron</span> pool in general.</li>\n<li>Increased rate of γ <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"29e1987f81169277719209260ba0f1\">motor neuron</span> discharge.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Producing a mid-collicular <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d5e7bb15851692777191b39417c26a\">lesion</span> in an <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"a9a33df37216927771877270a0f525\">experimental animal</span> results in decerebration.</p>\n<table cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:733px\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Feature</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Decerebrate Rigidity</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Decorticate Rigidity</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Definition</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>A state of severe <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"68f7148c4e1692777189074a8370ef\">hypertonia</span> characterized by extension of all four limbs.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>A state in which the upper extremities are flexed and the lower extremities are extended.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Cause</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Damage to the lower <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d26464df7216927771923483619265\">midbrain</span> and upper pons</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Damage to the upper midbrain</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Mechanism</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Loss of <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"0cf8ac70611692777186b133d027f6\">descending</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"f03ca2d2a716927771901227bc175a\">inhibition</span> to the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"a533b2d59f1692777196694dbb1b2a\">pontine</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"0b6b1f44cb1692777197afef785626\">reticular</span> system causes <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d92c42574616927771946db516e33e\">overactivity</span> of this system, which excites <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"e6f57b5b771692777181839b51f6ee\">antigravity</span> muscles.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Rubrospinal <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"1a1307223f16927772017a994bfc39\">tract</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"8265e091151692777187f264d73f3b\">excitation</span> of <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"3674af39031692777202252504982a\">flexor</span> muscles in the upper extremities results in <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"85ff8a7ff81692777202a827961a5c\">flexion</span> due to damage above the red nucleus.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Posture</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Arms adducted and extended</p>\n<p>Forearms pronated</p>\n<p>Wrists and fingers flexed</p>\n<p>Legs extended</p>\n<p>Feet <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"a7a430f3a9169277719510c13f434d\">plantar</span> flexed</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Arms adducted and flexed</p>\n<p>Wrists and fingers flexed</p>\n<p>Legs extended</p>\n<p>Plantar <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"85ff8a7ff81692777202a827961a5c\">flexion</span> of the feet</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Clinical Significance</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Severe <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"2fd6b3cdf516927771836603ca8c63\">brain stem</span> damage; poor prognosis</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Better <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"e580b4033e169277719609af594c16\">prognosis</span> than decerebrate rigidity</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p> </p>\n<p style=\"text-align:center\"><img alt=\"\" data-author=\"\" data-hash=\"\" data-license=\"\" data-source=\"\" data-tags=\"\" height=\"2488\" src=\"images/exp_110_199_1.jpg\" width=\"3598\"/></p><br/><img src=\"images/exp_110_199_1.jpg\"/><br/><br/><div class=\"quiz-references\">Ganong&rsquo;s Review of Medical Physiology, Edition 26, pg no 236-239.</div>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436539258","topic":"PrepLadder · 7.Previous Year Questions","number":5,"stem":"Which lobe is affected by a lesion that results in a deficit in hand-eye coordination?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Parietal lobe"},{"label":"B","text":"Frontal lobe"},{"label":"C","text":"Temporal lobe"},{"label":"D","text":"Occipital lobe"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Parietal lobe","solutionHtml":"<p>Impairment of hand-eye <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"3820ba101416927771858fe257e119\">coordination</span> is commonly associated with lesions in the brain’s <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"51df38de3d1692777194ced4c4bab5\">parietal</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d7dd6ae43c1692777191cf75c0bd58\">lobe</span> especially in the Brodmann area 5 and 7.</p>\n<p>The <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"51df38de3d1692777194ced4c4bab5\">parietal</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d7dd6ae43c1692777191cf75c0bd58\">lobe</span> integrates visual input from the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"77dc7a0ab81692777194dba7ab78ab\">occipital</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d7dd6ae43c1692777191cf75c0bd58\">lobe</span> and motor output from the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"35aa36279d16927772031c7ce8d6e5\">frontal</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d7dd6ae43c1692777191cf75c0bd58\">lobe</span> and acts as an association cortex.. It helps process and integrate <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"408bcde7f01692777198acadb8e1c6\">sensory</span> inputs to guide motor movements and coordinate hand-eye interactions and is the most important area</p>\n<div style=\"text-align:center\">\n<figure class=\"caption_element\" style=\"display:inline-block\"><img alt=\"Broadmanns-\" data-author=\"NA\" data-hash=\"12618\" data-license=\"NA\" data-source=\"NA\" data-tags=\"May2025\" height=\"666\" src=\"images/exp_118_111_1.jpg\" width=\"600\"/>\n<figcaption>{{caption_text}}</figcaption>\n</figure>\n</div>\n<h3><strong>Brodmann Areas: </strong></h3>\n<h3><strong>Definition</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Numbered regions of the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"ed2f4c790516927771840d0d99e9f4\">cerebral cortex</span> identified by Korbinian Brodmann, based on neuronal structure and arrangement.</li>\n<li>Linked to <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"408bcde7f01692777198acadb8e1c6\">sensory</span> processing, motor control, and cognitive functions.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Key Brodmann Areas and Functions</strong></p>\n<table cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:531px\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Brodmann Area</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Function</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>1, 2, 3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Primary <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"be46da176016927771984a269a5b2c\">somatosensory</span> cortex; processes <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"ff110f2cb71692777200a3483aa670\">tactile</span> information.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Primary motor cortex; controls voluntary movements.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>5, 7</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Somatosensory association areas; integrate <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"408bcde7f01692777198acadb8e1c6\">sensory</span> input.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>6</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Premotor/supplementary motor areas; plan movements.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>17</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Primary visual cortex; processes visual data.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>18, 19</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Visual association areas; advanced visual processing.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>22</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Wernicke's area; facilitates language comprehension.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>44, 45</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Broca's area; involved in speech production.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Frontal <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d7dd6ae43c1692777191cf75c0bd58\">lobe</span> (Option B):</strong> The <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"35aa36279d16927772031c7ce8d6e5\">frontal</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d7dd6ae43c1692777191cf75c0bd58\">lobe</span> is responsible for motor output and is involved in the hand-eye movements, but the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"51df38de3d1692777194ced4c4bab5\">parietal</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d7dd6ae43c1692777191cf75c0bd58\">lobe</span> is the most important.</p>\n<p><strong>Temporal <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d7dd6ae43c1692777191cf75c0bd58\">lobe</span> (Option C)</strong>: The <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"637ea4d17516927772003be2b2aae4\">temporal</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d7dd6ae43c1692777191cf75c0bd58\">lobe</span> is mainly associated with <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"f17057f75016927771829e70074368\">auditory</span> processing, memory, and language functions, and lesions in this <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d7dd6ae43c1692777191cf75c0bd58\">lobe</span> typically do not cause significant impairments in hand-eye coordination.</p>\n<p><strong>Occipital <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d7dd6ae43c1692777191cf75c0bd58\">lobe</span> (Option D):</strong> The <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"77dc7a0ab81692777194dba7ab78ab\">occipital</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d7dd6ae43c1692777191cf75c0bd58\">lobe</span> is primarily responsible for visual processing and is involved in the hand-eye movements, but the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"51df38de3d1692777194ced4c4bab5\">parietal</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d7dd6ae43c1692777191cf75c0bd58\">lobe</span> is the most important</p>\n<p> </p>\n<br/><img src=\"images/exp_118_111_1.jpg\"/><br/><br/><div class=\"quiz-references\">https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20483389/</div>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436539260","topic":"PrepLadder · 7.Previous Year Questions","number":6,"stem":"Which sensory receptors are accountable for tactile discrimination among the options provided? Merkel disc Ruffini end organ Pacinian corpuscle Meissner’s corpuscle","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1 and 4 are correct"},{"label":"B","text":"2 is correct"},{"label":"C","text":"3 is correct"},{"label":"D","text":"None are correct"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"1 and 4 are correct","solutionHtml":"<p>Tactile discrimination, which refers to the ability to discern fine details, textures, and shapes through touch, relies on <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"ebb480187d1692777199e233e9e356\">superficial</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"408bcde7f01692777198acadb8e1c6\">sensory</span> receptors in the skin.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>Both Merkel discs and Meissner’s corpuscles are involved in <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"ff110f2cb71692777200a3483aa670\">tactile</span> discrimination, allowing individuals to sense and distinguish intricate textures and shapes.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><strong>Specialized mechanoreceptors</strong></p>\n<p> </p>\n<table cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:NaN\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<figure class=\"caption_element\"><img alt=\"Meissners \" data-author=\"NA\" data-hash=\"12619\" data-license=\"NA\" data-source=\"NA\" data-tags=\"May2025\" src=\"images/exp_118_115_1.jpg\"/>\n<figcaption>{{caption_text}}</figcaption>\n</figure>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<figure class=\"caption_element\"><img alt=\"Merkel \" data-author=\"NA\" data-hash=\"12622\" data-license=\"NA\" data-source=\"NA\" data-tags=\"May2025\" src=\"images/exp_118_115_2.jpg\"/>\n<figcaption>{{caption_text}}</figcaption>\n</figure>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<figure class=\"caption_element\"><img alt=\"Pacinian \" data-author=\"NA\" data-hash=\"12623\" data-license=\"NA\" data-source=\"NA\" data-tags=\"May2025\" src=\"images/exp_118_115_3.jpg\"/>\n<figcaption>{{caption_text}}</figcaption>\n</figure>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<figure class=\"caption_element\"><img alt=\"Ruffini endings\" data-author=\"NA\" data-hash=\"12624\" data-license=\"NA\" data-source=\"NA\" data-tags=\"May2025\" src=\"images/exp_118_115_4.jpg\"/>\n<figcaption>{{caption_text}}</figcaption>\n</figure>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Superficial</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Superficial</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Deep</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Deep</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Discriminatory touch, Stroking</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Texture, Edges, Braille</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Pressure, Vibration</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Sustained pressure</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Rapidly adapting</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Slowly adapting</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Rapidly adapting</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Slowly adapting</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<br/><img src=\"images/exp_118_115_1.jpg\"/><br/><img src=\"images/exp_118_115_2.jpg\"/><br/><img src=\"images/exp_118_115_3.jpg\"/><br/><img src=\"images/exp_118_115_4.jpg\"/><br/><br/><div class=\"quiz-references\">Guyton and Hall Textbook of Medical Physiology, 14th edition, Page 599, 600</div>","tags":""}]}